  "body": "## What changed\n\nRequested in #192: \"features that are blocked seem to fail for no reason, until you realise there's feedback in the bottom left you've missed.\"\n\nThe status strip now reads its own line. A refusal is drawn so it cannot be missed - the palette's error ink (colour-vision aware), bold, behind a `!` marker, on an error-tinted band across the strip - until the next status replaces it. Ordinary status (saved, generated, ready) stays dim as before.\n\nWhat counts as a refusal (`egui_app/status_alert.rs::is_alert`):\n- the message `State::refuse` recorded (the feedback path - its message *is* the status);\n- a dark cell's gate note (`cannot …`);\n- the shell's own refusal phrasings set directly on the status: ` refused`, ` failed`, ` not set:`, ` not changed:`, ` not aligned:`, ` no longer `, `not generated`.\n\n**#215 folded in (second commit):** routine status is now drawn in the theme's body text ink instead of egui's dim \"weak\" grey (contrast-gated against the strip fill in both built-in themes), and \"not created:\" joins the refusal phrasings. Snapshots `egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png` move by the brighter status line (they overlap the other open UI PRs' snapshot changes). Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#192).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: every binary green except the lib's `egui_shell_snapshot_light` (Diff 1) and `tool_editor_snapshot` (Diff 4) - software-GL pixel diffs with the same counts on main on this machine. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::status_alert::tests::ordinary_status_is_not_an_alert`\n- `egui_app::status_alert::tests::refusals_are_alerts`\n- `egui_app::status_alert::tests::routine_status_ink_reads_on_the_strip` (#215: body-text contrast on the strip, dark and light)\n- `egui_app::status_alert::tests::a_command_refused_through_the_feedback_path_is_an_alert` (a refused delete through the real command drain; a later status retires the alert)\n\nChangelog: The status strip is readable (body ink) and a refused action's message is highlighted (error ink, \"!\" marker, tinted band)\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, merges at the next cut.\n\nFixes #192\nFixes #215\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
